description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/activity-lifecycle-audit.ts, make the lifecycle audit read the timestamp field that the execution-traces route actually emits, so recency stops being a constant.

Measured: the route emits `executed_at` on 800 of 800 rows, and emits none of `occurred_at`, `completed_at`, `started_at`, `created_at`. So traceTimestamp returns null for every row, bucket.newest stays null, ageDays defaults to 14, and recency is pinned at exp(-14/5)=0.061 for every template.

Two coupled edits, both required for the change to have any effect.

EDIT 1 — the interface. It currently contains this exact line:

  started_at?: unknown;

Immediately after that line, add:

  executed_at?: unknown;

EDIT 2 — the read. The file currently contains this exact block:

  if (typeof t.started_at === "string") {
    const v = Date.parse(t.started_at);
    if (!Number.isNaN(v)) return v;
  }

Immediately after that block, add:

  if (typeof t.executed_at === "string") {
    const v = Date.parse(t.executed_at);
    if (!Number.isNaN(v)) return v;
  }

Change nothing else in the file. Verified over 800 real rows: this takes null timestamps from 45/45 to 0/45, distinct recency values from 1 to 9, and distinct combined_score values from 6 to 11.

